{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CfQrZEtyd4nKZK5N3xxBk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Those two matches are this session's own driver and the shell running the check, not test processes. Nothing is left running from this iteration, and item 08 is still open so the loop is not complete.\n\nItem 07 (§2.6a, distil the closing policy) is **solved**.\n\n**What was wrong with the inherited code.** The earlier attempt's worker pool forked after LightGBM had run in the parent, so the children deadlocked in libgomp and the first run sat 15 minutes on sleeping workers. Its MCN tie-break also used total product count where `least_cost_node` uses products not yet produced. Both are fixed; the module's MCN now agrees with the solver's on all 1,920 held-out instances.\n\n**What was built.** `learning/distil.py` fits, per file-grouped fold, a depth-3 tree and a logistic scorer to the 2.24 M witness decisions, plus the same two fitted to the ranker's own scores, and evaluates all 570 lexicographic rules of up to three keys, Fiedler and BFS orders, and cs-dfs seeded three ways. Full run is about 4 minutes on 16 workers. `tests/test_distil.py` adds 11 hand-checkable tests. Full suite: 764 passed, 2 skipped, 1 xfailed.\n\n**The finding, in one paragraph.** The kill criterion (\"no readable rule keeps more than half the ranker's gain\") is exceeded in the opposite direction. The rule *close the customer that opens the fewest new stacks; on ties, the one with the most unclosed neighbours* scores held-out MAE 0.348 and exact 80.7% against the ranker's 0.519 and 75.0% and MCN's 1.616 and 50.2%. It keeps 115% of the ranker's gain, beats it in every size band and every collection but Shaw, and is worse on only 109 of 1,920 instances. The first key alone is the cheapest-first expansion order of Chu & Stuckey's own DFS, so the greedy is that search's first leaf. The tie-break is the reverse of MCN's minimum-degree criterion. As a DFS seed the rule also beats the learned order, at MCN's cost with no model. The distilled tree keeps 57%, the logistic scorer 82%, and imitation rate ranks constructions almost inversely to their value, which matters for item 08.\n\n**Files touched.** `learning/distil.py`, `tests/test_distil.py`, `reports/distil_tables.md`, `reports/ml_nature.md` §7, PROGRESS.md (now 7/8), iterations.md. Nothing written to `solutions/`, no solver defaults changed, no commits made, and the running recertify was not touched.\n\n**Next.** Item 08 (degeneracy of the optimum) is the last open item. The loop's owner should decide whether to register the rule as a heuristic in `satisfiability/heuristics.py` and measure it as the DFS seed against `learned+cs-dfs` in a corpus sweep."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":32,"cache_creation_input_tokens":399,"cache_read_input_tokens":166508,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":399,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":751,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"5a589f77-2584-4577-8831-52251d2454c1","uuid":"39d79f91-c2bf-41ee-9109-ef50c9bde90c","timestamp":"2026-09-25T21:19:12.644Z","request_id":"req_011CfQrZE9anknnNTjd3SfZ1"}
